<title>HUNGARY: FINMIN CONFIRMS 10BP/MTH CUT IN DEVALUATOR.</title>
<headline>FINMIN CONFIRMS 10BP/MTH CUT IN DEVALUATOR.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hungarian Finance Ministry's press department on Tuesday confirmed that the monthly crawling peg devaluator will be reduced to one percent from 1.1 percent as of August 15.</p>
<p>&quot;We confirm this news,&quot; a press department official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Hungarian news agency MTI quoted Finance Minister Peter Medgyessy earlier today as saying that the monthly crawling peg devaluator will be reduced to one percent from that date.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
